  "notes": "Source: official SDSU 'Computer Science (BS) 2025-2026 Sample Plan' PDF (2 pages, archived May 2025 on sdstate.edu), linked from the catalog's Academic Advising Guide Sheet for the B.S. in Computer Science. Program requirement list cross-checked against the catalog program page (catalog.sdstate.edu, 'Program: Computer Science (B.S.)', Bachelor of Science, 120 credits: System Gen Ed 33 + Major Requirements 71 + Supporting Coursework 16). Transcription: pdftotext of the official PDF, transcribed verbatim term-by-term; course titles and prerequisites taken exactly as printed in the plan's Course Title / Prerequisites-Comments columns. Semester totals re-summed from plan data and match the printed totals (15/16/16/16/15/15/15/12 = 120). 'p. Placement' prerequisite details (ENGL 101, MATH 123) recorded here rather than in external_prereqs. 'p. MATH 103 or higher' for STAT 281 is represented as plain code MATH 103 in external_prereqs. Caveats: (1) The 2025-2026 plan is the newest official CS sample plan found; no 2026-2027 CS plan exists in SDSU's file archive (2026-2027 plans exist only for other programs). The current catalog page lists some updated numbering (MATH 270 Computational Linear Algebra vs the plan's MATH 250 Introduction to Linear Algebra and Proof; CSC 464/465 as 2 credits each vs 3 in the plan; titles CSC 484 'Database Management Systems' vs plan's 'Database Management'; STAT 281 'Introduction to Statistics' vs plan's 'Statistical Methods I'; CSC 303 'Ethical and Security Issues in Computing' vs plan's '...in Computer Science'). Transcribed the plan as printed since it is the genuine official term-by-term sequence. (2) The plan places CSC 303 and CSC 317 in Fall Year 2 while its own Semester column marks both as spring-offered (S); transcribed placement as printed. (3) The plan is a sample: 'Students are not limited to this plan; it is meant to be used as a guide for planning purposes in consultation with your advisor.' (4) CSC and SE courses require a grade of C or better; graduating seniors take the Major Field Test in Computer Science. (5) SE 305/306 are marked fall/spring only in the plan's Semester column (F/S respectively), consistent with their placement.",
